; loop_stack_overflow: loop nesting is capped at 8192 frames.
;
; RANGE and ITER each push a loop frame and only NEXT pops one, so a
; program that jumps back over a loop header without running its NEXT
; grows the loop stack without bound. A LoopFrame is not charged against
; the allocation budget either, so nothing else bounded it: this six
; instruction program grew the stack until the host ran out of memory.
;
; The cap mirrors the 8192-element value-stack limit that has been in
; place since the first release.

TARGET .0
PUSH 0
PUSH 2
RANGE
JUMP .0
